  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1123 AM MDT Fri May 8 2026\n\nSmall upper low well south of the NM Bootheel currently, and is\nslowly drifting east-northeast, reaching the Big Bend this\nevening. Cold pool aloft associated with the low also remains well\nsouth of us through tonight. Despite that, modest instability\nnumbers develop this afternoon over northern Mexico and west\nTexas. LI's of 0 to -2 and MUCAPES of around 200 J/kg develop this\nafternoon and early evening, so low POPs over southern Hudspeth\nthis afternoon and early evening look warranted. \n\nLow exits the region late tonight and the general pattern into the\nmid portion of next week is for ridging to build in over the\nDesert Southwest for a mainly dry solution. A short wave from the\nnorthern Rockies does drop down across eastern New Mexico Sunday.\nModels have been backing off some on POPs, but it still looks like\neastern Otero (Sacs) and maybe eastern Hudspeth could see some\nshowers Sunday afternoon into early evening. Decent CAPE values\neast of the Rio Grande suggest thunderstorms far eastern sections. \n\nUpper ridge drifts over New Mexico Monday through Wednesday with\ncontinued above normal temperatures. GFS/ECMWF continue to show\nsub-tropical tap streaming up the west side of the ridge over\nArizona in increasing southerly flow Wednesday. Could see a few\nshowers Wednesday west of the Cont Divide. Models then take the\ntrough/moisture plume east across the CWA Thursday for a brief\nslight chance of showers, though this not reflected in grids at\nthis time. Models do seem to be trending down with this event too.",
